# Example config for claude-notify-resume.
#
# Copy to ~/.claude/claude-notify-resume.conf and uncomment what you want.
# Nothing here is required — every line has a sensible default.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, # starts a comment. Unknown keys are ignored.
# Each key also works as an environment variable prefixed CLAUDE_NOTIFY_, which
# takes precedence over this file.

# Statuses to drop, comma-separated. Case and spaces around commas don't matter.
# Valid names: Replied, Permission needed, Waiting for you, Input needed,
#              Background agent needs you, Background agent finished
#
# `Replied` fires on every reply — useful when you have walked away, noisy when
# you are watching the chat.
#
# MUTE=Replied,Waiting for you

# Where a click reopens the session. Detected from the process tree by default;
# set this only if the guess is wrong.
#   Terminal — Terminal.app (the fallback)
#   iTerm    — iTerm2
#   vscode   — open the folder in VS Code instead of resuming in a terminal
#
# TERMINAL=iTerm
